infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When the mapping tax pays off
  desc Clean Architecture earns its cost only under specific forces
  compares
    - label Worth it
      children
        - label Long-lived, complex domain
          desc Invariants grow over years; the entity core has real rules to protect
        - label 3+ delivery mechanisms
          desc Web, mobile, partner API, CLI all reuse the same interactors
        - label Teams that grow and change
          desc Explicit contracts outlast any one engineer's knowledge
    - label Overkill
      children
        - label Thin CRUD apps
          desc Entities are data bags — no invariants for the pure core to protect
        - label Short-lived or throwaway
          desc Rebuilt before the long-term payoff ever accrues
        - label No boundary discipline
          desc Tax is permanent; the guarantee dies on one framework import
theme
  palette #10b981 #f43f5e
